---
description: How to behave when armord blocks or holds a tool call
alwaysApply: true
---

armord checks shell, MCP, file-read and write calls before they run.

- When a call is denied, do not retry it, reword it, or reach the same effect through another tool.
  Tell the user what was denied and the reason shown.
- When Cursor asks the user to approve a call, wait for the answer.
- Never edit `.cursor/hooks.json`, `.cursor/mcp.json`, or anything under `~/.armoriq/`.
- Before a multi-step task you may call the `register_intent_plan` tool (server `armord-plan`) with
  the tools you intend to use; calls outside that plan are refused.
